@Gov_WebApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5049

# Entra ID app registrations (created for OAuth-secured testing):
#   API app (exposes scope):  560b8b70-4f6f-4b63-8bc5-a5980b9a3db5  (api://560b8b70-4f6f-4b63-8bc5-a5980b9a3db5)
#   Client app (calls API):   dacb53be-6a39-4918-b5a1-b994a625252e  (public client, redirect http://localhost)
#   Scope:                    api://560b8b70-4f6f-4b63-8bc5-a5980b9a3db5/Mcp.Access
#   Tenant:                   2d71cc54-bc9e-4518-aebc-618c6aa63f9a
#
# Get a token (device code flow) with the Azure CLI, then paste it into @token below:
#   az login --tenant 2d71cc54-bc9e-4518-aebc-618c6aa63f9a --allow-no-subscriptions --use-device-code
#   az account get-access-token --scope "api://560b8b70-4f6f-4b63-8bc5-a5980b9a3db5/Mcp.Access" --query accessToken -o tsv
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing with a NEW app registration in a DIFFERENT tenant that has no exposed
# scope yet (nothing added under "Expose an API"):
#   1. Set Gov.WebApi/appsettings.Development.json -> Authentication:TenantId /
#      Authentication:ApiClientId to the new tenant/app IDs (this file overrides
#      appsettings.json when running locally, ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development).
#   2. Because no scope is exposed, request a plain v1-style token for the app
#      itself using --resource instead of --scope (no "api://" App ID URI needed):
#        az login --tenant <NEW_TENANT_ID> --allow-no-subscriptions --use-device-code
#        az account get-access-token --resource <NEW_APP_CLIENT_ID> --query accessToken -o tsv
#   3. Program.cs now accepts both v2.0 tokens (aud=api://ClientId, iss=.../v2.0) and
#      v1.0 tokens obtained this way (aud=ClientId, iss=https://sts.windows.net/TENANT/),
#      and the McpAccess policy only requires an authenticated user (no scp check), so
#      this works even though no Mcp.Access scope has been defined.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Health check (public, no auth required)
GET {{Gov_WebApi_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Get projects (REST API, requires OAuth bearer token + Mcp.Access scope)
GET {{Gov_WebApi_HostAddress}}/api/project
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### MCP endpoint (requires OAuth bearer token + Mcp.Access scope)
POST {{Gov_WebApi_HostAddress}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "tools/list"
}

### Swagger UI docs (public)
GET {{Gov_WebApi_HostAddress}}/docs

### ReDoc reference (public)
GET {{Gov_WebApi_HostAddress}}/reference
